step	13	-	Quick guide step 13
line	<str>To begin, sail to Wyrmscraig, found slightly south-west of Charred Island. Be sure not to bring a sloop, as it will not fit in a cave entered later in the quest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Dock at the island and try to run onto the island, and you will be stopped by Ffion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Run to Auchrie and speak to Cormac in the centre hut.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Muriel in the building immediately north-east of Cormac's hut, then run to the closest area marked on the map with the Mining icon.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the tent for a pickaxe, hammer, and chisel if needed, then inspect the sunstone monolith.</str>
line	
line	<str>Mine a piece off the sunstone monolith, and chisel it into a sunstone core. The scrawled notebook may be dropped.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the trail of dust to the south-west tip of the island and investigate the large hat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head back to Cormac and speak to him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Sail into Wyrmscraig Cavern on the south-west side of the island with either a skiff or raft.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the three mountain trolls nearest to Mortimer in the cavern. The area is multicombat, lower levelled players may consider praying Protect from Melee.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Mortimer again, then follow the path north until you see a golem. (You may exit the cave, via the western exit from the north path, to mine the rocks to the far east of the exit to gain access to the agility shortcut for ease of access to the cathedral later)</str>
line	
line	<str>Investigate the golem, use the sunstone core you mined on the golem, then open the chest inside the room (combination: right, left, down, down).</str>
